{"id": "EUVD-2026-42569", "enisaUuid": "627564d3-798c-3ad9-a778-57bfa0f1042d", "description": "A heap buffer overflow vulnerability was found in GStreamer's rfbsrc plugin. When a client connects to a malicious RFB/VNC server that advertises a 16bpp framebuffer and sends Hextile-encoded updates, the Hextile background fill path writes 32-bit pixel values into a buffer allocated for 16-bit pixels. This type mismatch causes an out-of-bounds heap write that can lead to denial of service (process crash) and potential memory corruption.", "datePublished": "2026-07-09T09:34:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-10T14:43:34", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:47179", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:47180", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:47731", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:54658", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:54659", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:54660", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:54664", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:54665", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:54752", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:56658", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:56772", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:62532", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-59691", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2497343", "https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer-security/-/merge_requests/100", "https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/work_items/5173"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-59691", "GHSA-g4ff-54hw-hj6r"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03830328-0905-37f5-9977-6b27bfb77f06", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8.6 Advanced Mission Critical Update Support", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.16.1-4.el8_6.4"}, {"id": "0fbcb278-7e50-3438-9868-3